    "id": "lem:step-indexed-ledger-positivity",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "statement": "At \\(p_H=O_H(\\theta)\\) for every \\(\\theta\\in\\Theta_H\\), every entry of the step-indexed ledger is strictly positive.  Hence every division made by context initialization, \\(\\operatorname{TF}_{\\prec}\\), or computed fixing is legal, and every returned formula satisfies \\(O_H(\\Theta_H)\\subseteq\\mathfrak D_H\\).  No common numerical lower bound is asserted.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "posLedgerH",
      "pH",
      "OH",
      "ThetaH",
      "Cadm",
      "H",
      "S",
      "TFH",
      "FixH",
      "dH",
      "DH"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "ass:exact-selector-support",
      "ass:admissible-cell-interior",
      "def:step-indexed-ledger",
      "def:circuit-domain",
      "lem:context-construction-soundness",
      "lem:truncated-factorization-identity",
      "lem:computed-fixing-soundness"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "We induct on the ledger index.  For a base entry at \\(s\\in H\\),\n\\[\n p_H(S=s)=\\sum_{v:(v,s)\\in\\mathcal C_H^{\\mathrm{adm}}(G^{+})}p_H(v,s)>0\n\\tag{5}\n\\]\nby exact selector support and admissible-cell positivity.  Suppose all earlier entries are positive.  A conditioning marginal introduced by \\(\\operatorname{TF}_{\\prec}\\) is, by construction, a nonempty sum of cells of the current positive kernel.  A fixing conditional is constructed from current-kernel marginals, and its recorded numerator is likewise a nonempty sum.  After substituting the current kernel's rational expression in \\(p_H\\), the verifier records the exact factorization\n\\[\n d_j=c_j\\prod_{i<j}d_i^{m_{ij}}prod_{r=1}^{R_j}\n       \\left(\\sum_{c\\in C_{jr}}K_{jr}(c)\\right),\n\\qquad c_j\\in\\mathbb Q_{>0},\\quad C_{jr}\\ne\\varnothing,\n\\tag{6}\n\\]\nafter cancellation and sign normalization.  Every earlier factor is positive by induction, and every last sum is positive because its cells are branch-reachable positive kernel cells.  Thus \\(d_j>0\\).  This proves the induction.\n\nThe terminal denominator registry is a sublist of the ledger, so all its entries are positive at \\(O_H(\\theta)\\).  Required observed cells are positive by the model class.  The definition of \\(\\mathfrak D_H\\) now gives \\(O_H(\\Theta_H)\\subseteq\\mathfrak D_H\\).  Because the argument uses only strict inequalities at the fixed law, it supplies no uniform lower bound.",
